The results from this analysis show no evidence for critical fluctuations or anomalous event classes, but do find significant non-statistical fluctuations. Fixed target heavy ion experiments at the CERN SPS using a 158 GeV per nucleon Pb beam (\(\sqrt{s_{NN}}\approx 17\) GeV) measure much smaller values of transverse momentum

