### Track Selection

Once events have been chosen, it is necessary to select tracks from these events for use in forming pairs. In general, the favored approach is to minimally-bias the track sample by requiring only basic reconstruction quality over as large a kinematic range as possible. Table 5.4 gives a complete list of track cuts used in these analyses. Many of these cuts are shown in figure 5.4 where accepted tracks are shown as red histograms and combined accepted and rejected tracks are shown in black. Track cuts fall into three categories: kinematics, reconstruction, and particle identification.

